    "### 6.2 Governance notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key assumptions for Phase 3 ECL:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **EAD is deterministic:** Not modeled probabilistically. EAD = principal outstanding at default, observed from historical data.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **LGD and EAD are independent:** Correlation ≈ 0.08 (not significant). Segmentation can treat them separately.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Cure is implicit in PD:** Loans that cure have realized LGD = 0. The LGD model is calibrated only on defaults.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Vintage effects matter:** EAD varies by origination year (2013-2017 span). Phase 3 should validate vintage-level assumptions.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Macro sensitivity deferred:** Recovery rates (LGD) may worsen under recession. Stress scenarios are Phase 3 responsibility."
